    "preflight": [
      "Validate all pinned inputs/inherited sources and saved same-data v3 fingerprint before any fit.",
      "Regenerate independent random signs with the frozen source manifest seed/order/ramp/RMS formula. Require exact audit, clipping identities and recording alignment. Never center, rebalance, redraw, substitute realized injection or filter clipped rows.",
      "Rebuild all window keys, histories, applied commands, targets and raw current assignments from recordings; compare training/development arrays and roles to the saved same-data baseline cache. No reserved or response-diagnostic row can enter fitting or checkpoint selection.",
      "Fresh causal public-equation replay of all four calibration command trajectories in source float64 runtime, with absolute tolerance1e-10 and relative1e-12. Exact source pin/spec/initial state and command. This permits only numerical boundary roundoff, not trajectory changes.",
      "Check declared input-only excitation diagnostics before fitting. At least4origins per retained instrument direction in both fitting roles. Per raw command RMS>0; realized/requested RMS>=0.5; every phi-squared-weighted mean(requested*realized)/mean(requested^2)>=0.25. These are provisional support screens, not proof of identification. Save all values and ranks; no tuning/recollection after failure."
    ]
  },
  "mechanism": {
    "model": "Same filter_mlp architecture and initialization as adopted v3, trained in float64; final runtime predictions default float32.",
    "history_features": "Flatten exactly the consumed pre-command observed states and past applied commands; concatenate. Standardize each coordinate with training-only mean and standard deviation; use scale1 when standard deviation<=1e-8. No future observations, current assignment, future commands, model memory or outputs enter the feature map.",
    "feature_projection": {
      "seed": 0,
      "columns": 8,
      "distribution": "numpy.random.default_rng(0).normal(size=(D,8))/sqrt(D)",
      "map": "phi=[1,tanh(standardized_history @ W)]"
    },
    "instruments": "Z = outer(raw_current_requested_assignment / training_assignment_RMS, phi(history)), flattened by command then feature. Raw assignments are explicitly declared conditionally zero-mean requests before clipping; model inputs remain applied commands.",
    "projection": "Thin NumPy SVD of each role Z independently, using the same train-only history transform and assignment scales. Retain singular directions strictly greater than1e-6*largest singular value. Store singular values, retained rank, condition and Q. No target-dependent whitening, fitted history basis or rank tuning.",
    "singular_relative_cutoff": 1e-06,
    "conditional_loss": "R=(complete model first-step prediction - observed next state)/existing v3 loss_scale[0]. Identification loss=sum((Q.T@R)^2)/(N*output_channels). Total training objective=unchanged minibatch full-prefix MSE + full-batch conditional loss with coefficient1.0. First-step predictor receives only first future command. Gradients traverse all linear/nonlinear/memory parameters; phi and Q are fixed.",
    "coefficient": 1.0,
    "checkpoint": "Existing steps0,100,...1000. Select minimum development full-prefix MSE + development conditional moment, earliest on ties. Report both terms, initial and selected moments, every checkpoint. No held-out response scores affect selection.",
    "unchanged_optimizer": "1000Adamsteps, minibatch64, learning_rate0.002, gradientclip5, beta0.9/0.999, epsilon1e-8, seed0, existing ridge/init/loss scales; unchanged full-prefix normalization.",
    "undeclared_assignment": "Exactly zero conditional term and delegate to unmodified existing fitter; never infer randomization from a command waveform or generic excitation field.",
    "causal_limits": "Requires independent current assignment given pre-command history/plant innovations, exclusion through recorded applied commands, and an adequate conditional structural/mean model. Hidden effect modifiers or omitted history can invalidate this moment even with randomization. Finite27directions need not identify the full nonlinear response. Keep the moment one-step because later factual commands arose in feedback. Held-out response, not reduced moment, decides progress.",
    "primary_research_reference": "https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2019/file/15d185eaa7c954e77f5343d941e25fbd-Paper.pdf"
  },
  "arms": {
